  <title>Voice sets</title>
  <p>
    A voice set contains four voice types: default, uppercase, hyperlink, and system. The
    "Global" voice set normally applies. You can also create voice sets for other languages and
    configure each voice type separately.
  </p>
  <p>
    The default voice is used for presenting on-screen objects and text. The uppercase voice
    identifies capital letters, the hyperlink voice identifies links, and the system voice
    presents information supplied by Orca, such as roles, states, and messages. All four
    initially sound the same. Any voice type you have not explicitly configured uses the default
    voice's settings.
  </p>
  <p>
    See
    "<link xref="features_speech_and_voices_global_voice_settings">Global voice settings</link>"
    for behavior shared by all voice types and
    "<link xref="features_speech_and_voices_language_switching">Language switching</link>" for
    automatic and manual switching between voice sets.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-voice-sets">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Speech</gui> category, <gui>Voice Sets</gui> group.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Voice Sets</gui>: Lists the "Global" voice set and any language-specific voice
          sets.
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Voice set:</gui> Selects the voice set to review or change.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>New Voice Set</gui>: Creates a voice set for a specific language.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Remove</gui>: Removes the selected language-specific voice set.
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Voice Type Settings</gui>: Lists the voice types in the selected voice set.
          Activate the settings button for a voice type to change how that voice sounds.
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Language:</gui> Selects the language for the selected voice type. Available
              languages come from the voices reported by the current synthesizer.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Person:</gui> Selects the synthesizer voice for the selected voice type.
              Choices depend on the current synthesizer and selected language. If an installed
              voice is missing, check that it is available through the selected speech system
              and synthesizer and that its language is selected.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Rate:</gui> Sets the speech rate for the selected voice type (0-100).
              Default: 50.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Pitch:</gui> Sets the pitch for the selected voice type (0.0-10.0). Default:
              5.0.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Inflection:</gui> Sets the pitch variation for the selected voice type
              (0.0-10.0). Default: 5.0.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Volume:</gui> Sets the volume for the selected voice type (0.0-10.0).
              Default: 10.0.
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
  <section id="commands-voice-parameters">
    <title>Commands</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
